From: Ze kernel maintainers
Subject: [PATCH 11c] ppp: delete only the retained original address pair

Apply after canonical0007..0011a and frozen0011b. Owner-tagged address
deletion requires exact LOCAL/ADDRESS/prefix under the native writer locks.
IPv4 uses native secondary promotion without altering any configuration.
IPv6 checks the stored effective peer before native deletion. Untagged
selectors/promotion and all supported prefix lengths remain unchanged.
Bit10 is declared by unit51/global42 only with built-in supported families;
bit9 remains separately reserved for complete control-socket enforcement.

diff --git a/include/uapi/linux/ppp-ioctl.h b/include/uapi/linux/ppp-ioctl.h
--- a/include/uapi/linux/ppp-ioctl.h
+++ b/include/uapi/linux/ppp-ioctl.h
@@ -111,6 +111,8 @@
 #define PPP_OWNER_CONNECT (1U << 6)
 #define PPP_OWNER_BRIDGE  (1U << 7)
 #define PPP_OWNER_CAPTURE (1U << 8)
+/* Bit9 is reserved for complete control-socket enforcement. */
+#define PPP_OWNER_EXACT_ADDR_PAIR (1U << 10)
 
 /* Invoke on a bound /dev/ppp channel; fd names a held peer file, not an ID. */
 struct ppp_fd_peer {
